<title>JAPAN: Kyocera up on change of trading unit.</title>
<headline>Kyocera up on change of trading unit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kyocera Corp rose on Wednesday morning, helped by the firm's announcement on Tuesday that it plans to change its stock trading unit to 100 shares from 1,000 shares on February 3, 1997, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price of the ceramic maker was up 70 yen at 7,910 yen at 0107 GMT, on volume of 244,000 shares.</p>
<p>Kyocera said on Tuesday that the move was aimed at widening the firm's range of investors.</p>
</text>
